GNU Scientific Library Bessel routines
-------------------------------------

src/bessel_i.c adapts portions of these files from GNU Scientific Library
(GSL) version 2.8:

* specfunc/bessel_Inu.c
  Copyright (C) 1996, 1997, 1998, 1999, 2000 Gerard Jungman
* specfunc/bessel.c
  Copyright (C) 1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003 Gerard Jungman

Both files identify G. Jungman as the author and grant permission under
the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version. Their
copyright and license notices are also retained in src/bessel_i.c.

The pre-existing Bessel routines in src/INLAcirc_common.h are adapted from
the following GSL 2.8 sources and retain the same license:

* specfunc/bessel_I0.c: bi0_data, ai0_data, ai02_data and scaled I0 evaluation
  Copyright (C) 1996, 1997, 1998, 1999, 2000 Gerard Jungman
* specfunc/bessel_I1.c: bi1_data, ai1_data, ai12_data and scaled I1 evaluation
  Copyright (C) 1996, 1997, 1998, 1999, 2000 Gerard Jungman
* specfunc/bessel.c: gsl_sf_bessel_I_CF1_ser continued fraction
  Copyright (C) 1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003 Gerard Jungman
* specfunc/bessel_In.c: integer-order backward recurrence
  Copyright (C) 1996, 1997, 1998, 1999, 2000 Gerard Jungman

These coefficients use the INLAcirc_ prefix in the package. Their numerical
values are unchanged; copyright and GPL notices were added to the package
header. The separate src-cloglike copy was not modified.

Source release: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gsl/gsl-2.8.tar.gz
Archive SHA-256:
6a99eeed15632c6354895b1dd542ed5a855c0f15d9ad1326c6fe2b2c9e423190

The package includes selected Taylor-series, continued-fraction and uniform
asymptotic routines, adapted to a package-local C interface. The adaptation
uses the C mathematical library for the log-gamma prefactor and returns
results without calling GSL's error handler. No system GSL library or headers
are required. The standalone src-cloglike directory is not part of this
adaptation and is excluded from the R source package.

