Normal quantile approximation
-----------------------------

INLAcirc_qnorm in src/INLAcirc_common.h implements Peter John Acklam's
rational approximation to the standard-normal quantile, using the
coefficients and branch points in his original description:

Peter John Acklam, "An algorithm for computing the inverse normal
cumulative distribution function", first published in 2003 and last
updated 2010-01-21.

Original page: http://home.online.no/~pjacklam/notes/invnorm/
Archived page (permission verified 2026-10-05):
https://web.archive.org/web/20151030215612/http://home.online.no/~pjacklam/notes/invnorm/

The author's Computer implementations section states:
"Use them as you wish, for whatever purpose."
His copyright FAQ explicitly extends this permission to the algorithm and
listed implementations, and requests that credit be given. Peter John
Acklam is credited here as the author of the approximation. The package
does not designate this upstream permission as an MIT license or claim
that Acklam waived copyright.

R-INLA interface declarations and PC-prior reference formulas
------------------------------------------------------------

src/INLAcirc_cgeneric_compat.h contains the subset of declarations needed
for the external cloglike ABI from R-INLA's inlaprog/src/cgeneric.h.

The small-concentration and asymptotic PC-prior formulas in
src/INLAcirc_common.h correspond to rinla/R/pc-vm0.R and
rinla/R/pc-vminf.R. Both reference files credit Xiang Ye as their author.
The package evaluates these formulas in C and does not execute R-INLA's
R implementations for these calculations.

